---
// The privacy page: what the site keeps, in plain English, accurate to the
// code (ARCHITECTURE.md §8, §19). A first draft for the owner to review; not
// legal advice. Keep it in step with the code: a change to what's stored,
// logged or measured changes this page too.
import Page from "../layouts/Page.astro";
import { CORRECTIONS_EMAIL } from "../config";
import { FRIENDLY_PATH } from "../lib/paths";

const TURNSTILE_ADDENDUM = "https://www.cloudflare.com/en-gb/turnstile-privacy-policy/";
---

<Page
  title="Privacy: No Cookies, No Accounts, No Ads | Bigger Than Game"
  description="What Bigger Than Game keeps and why: no cookies, no accounts and no ads. Your best score stays in your browser and game stats are anonymous. In plain English."
  stickyBar
>
  <h1>Privacy</h1>
  <p>
    Bigger Than Game is built to know as little about you as possible. This page sets out everything
    the site keeps, where it's kept and for how long.
  </p>

  <h2>The short version</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>No cookies, no accounts and no sign-up.</li>
    <li>No advertising, and nothing that tracks you from site to site.</li>
    <li>Your best score is kept in your own browser, not by us.</li>
    <li>Game statistics are anonymous: the only thing about you they record is your country.</li>
    <li>
      Feedback you send is emailed to us and also kept in our server logs for three days. Please
      don't include personal details in it.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>In your browser</h2>
  <p>
    Your best score is saved in your browser's local storage, one number per game mode, so the game
    can show it next time and tell you when you've beaten it. It never leaves your device, and
    clearing this site's data in your browser removes it. We don't set any cookies.
  </p>

  <h2>When you play</h2>
  <p>
    The game asks our server for each question as you go, so that the hidden number isn't sent to
    your browser before you've answered. Like every website, the server sees your IP address when
    your browser connects. We use it for one thing: limiting how fast a single connection can play,
    to stop anyone copying the game's data. The limit forgets it within a minute, and it never goes
    into our logs or statistics.
  </p>
  <p>
    To see how the game plays and keep it fair, the server records anonymous game events: when a run
    starts and ends, and for each answer the question number, the stat, whether it was right and the
    score. Each event carries the country your connection comes from (as Cloudflare reports it) and
    a random run number made for that run alone. There's no IP address, no details of your device or
    browser, and nothing that links one run to another or to you. These events are kept for three
    months.
  </p>

  <h2>Server logs</h2>
  <p>
    For three days, our server logs keep a short record of what happened: the start and end of each
    run (with the country, the score and the question that ended it), requests the server refused,
    and errors. Cloudflare can also log every request automatically, with its IP address and browser
    details; we've switched that off.
  </p>

  <h2>Feedback forms</h2>
  <p>
    The forms, <a href={`${FRIENDLY_PATH}#suggest`}>Suggest a legend</a>,{" "}
    <a href={`${FRIENDLY_PATH}#problem`}>Report a problem</a> and the report on a card at the end of
    a run, send us what you type: the legend's name and your note, your note and the page you were
    on, or your note and the two players, the stat and the figures on that card. None of the forms
    asks for your email address or any other details, and we'd ask you not to put any in.
  </p>
  <p>
    What you send is emailed to us, and we keep the email for as long as we need it to act on what
    you've told us. A copy is kept in our server logs for three days, with your country and nothing
    else about you.
  </p>

  <h3>Cloudflare Turnstile</h3>
  <p>
    Before a form sends, Cloudflare Turnstile checks that it's being sent by a person and not a bot.
    It loads only when you open a form, never while you're just playing. To make that check,
    Cloudflare processes your IP address, details of your connection and your browser's user agent,
    to detect and block bots, under the{" "}
    <a href={TURNSTILE_ADDENDUM}>Cloudflare Turnstile Privacy Addendum</a>. We receive only whether
    the check passed.
  </p>

  <h2>Visit counts</h2>
  <p>
    We use Cloudflare Web Analytics to count visits: how many people view each page, where they
    arrived from, and their country and type of device, all in total. It doesn't use cookies or
    anything else stored in your browser, and it doesn't follow you across sites.
  </p>

  <h2>Who runs the site</h2>
  <p>
    Cloudflare hosts the site and runs its server, and serves the player photos from our own image
    address. The fonts are served by the site itself, so pages don't contact any font service. The
    link to GitHub in the footer takes you to GitHub, which has its own privacy policy.
  </p>

  <h2>No advertising or tracking</h2>
  <p>
    There are no adverts, no advertising or social media trackers, and no data sold or passed to
    anyone for marketing.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about this page, or about anything you've sent us? Email us at{" "}
    <a href={`mailto:${CORRECTIONS_EMAIL}`}>{CORRECTIONS_EMAIL}</a>.
  </p>
</Page>
